# Enabled Haraka plugins, in order. Keep this minimal — the edge is a dumb pipe.

# Reject RCPT for any domain not accepted by the platform (anti-open-relay). Live lookup
# against the Worker's GET /api/mx/accepted-domains, with a short-TTL in-memory cache and a
# re-check on cache miss, so a freshly-verified domain is accepted on its first message —
# no host_list sync/cron/restart needed. config/host_list is now only a cold-start seed.
mailkite_rcpt

# Edge verdicts → emitted as x-mailkite-* headers by mailkite_ingest, stored by the
# Worker. SPF + DKIM verify run standalone (no daemon). DMARC has no bundled plugin
# (derived later). rspamd needs a running rspamd daemon — enable in prod once available.
spf
dkim
#rspamd

# Inbound spam SIGNAL only — a DNSBL lookup on the connecting IP, which is the one spam
# input the Worker cannot compute (by /api/ingest the TCP peer is us). It has NO reject
# path: spam is a flag, never a gate — docs/architecture/inbound-spam.md §1. Fails open to
# `unknown` (never `clean`) on any config/resolver/timeout failure.
mailkite_spam

# STARTTLS. Reads certs from config/tls/ (tls_cert.pem + tls_key.pem), placed there by
# /usr/local/bin/mailkite-mta-tls-deploy.sh on issue and on every renewal — see
# config/tls.ini and README §TLS. Without it the edge accepts mail in the clear.
tls

# The bridge: queue hook → HMAC POST to the Worker ingest.
mailkite_ingest
